 tempting to visit the fridge  or grab something from the food cupboard  i mean have you actually counted how  many times you have  opened and closed your fridge and food  cupboard well  start counting and let me know in the  comments below  to fight against this you have to find a  different activity to get outside  the boredom zone immediately if i find  myself  sitting on the couch for more than half  an hour munching away  i will force myself to get up and put on  a workout video from phil  and start working out it's only a 30  minute workout  but it always makes me feel so much  better afterwards  i'm burning and not consuming more  calories  i would also spend time playing with my  dog rusty  and also do some reading to keep myself  and my brain occupied  i think this is in fact the best time  for you to pick up a new hobby of skills  and improve yourself so there's really  no excuses of feeling  bored and just wasting your time away  now that you're spending a lot of time  at home with your family and probably  cooking a lot more often  this can also lead to overeating i mean  come on mom's home-cooked meals  are the best everyone is enjoying it and  we have to finish it  just to keep her happy let's face it  sometimes  our own family members can be an  unintentional saboteur  by encouraging us to keep eating and  eating come on eat more darling i made  these cookies and these buns  you got to try them they're delicious  eat  keep finishing it yes if you have such  friends or family members you need to  learn when to say  no and that you have had enough of food  it will be challenging especially to  your family  but if you can have an open conversation  with them and share with them  your fitness goals then perhaps they can  be more understanding  and supportive towards you  ladies you know very well what i'm  talking about you've been eating  so well and a few days right before your  period  bam your hormone changes and you  suddenly crave for  all the bad stuff this is so me in fact  it just happened to me a couple of days  ago  i lost control and just wanted sweet  desserts  savory snacks and nothing seemed to  satisfy me  and i ended up with a bloated tummy you  don't have to deprive yourself but what  is important is that you're aware of  the hormonal changes that are happening  in your body  so when you indulge eat in a mindful way  and enjoy your food with all your senses  you will feel satisfied with less  and you will be in control of the  situation soon  the cravings will start to fade away and  you'll find balance again  for the next three days i want you to  record every single thing you eat  and then determine what kind of hunger  it was ask yourself  why did you eat were you physically  hungry or were you just stressed or  bored  was it a habit-based decision or because  everyone else was eating  write it down and share your thoughts  with me in the comments below  by recognizing which hunger you're  experiencing you'll be able to take the  right approach  to satisfy it and stop overeating  eventually  you'll be in control of your eating  habits rather than allowing your  emotions or surroundings  to control you so let me know your  experience and thoughts  in the comments below if you find these  tips to be useful then  do give this video a thumbs up share it  on with your family members and friends  and do also hit the subscribe button if  you haven't yet subscribed  check out my youtube channel for a lot  more home workout videos  healthy recipes and also meal plans to  help you get started in  your fitness journey and i will see you  in my next video  all the best


